---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Cristian Serrano - Digital Product Designer"
  description="Who Cristian Serrano is beyond the work: curiosity-driven, always learning, Head of Design at JustRelate -- what he looks for in a team, and what he brings to it."
>
  <header>
    <h1>Hi! I'm Cristian :) </h1>
    <p>I'm a digital product designer with <span id="experienceYears"></span> of experience who enjoys the challenge of making the complex simple.</p>
  </header>

  <hr>

  <section id="about-me">

    <h2>So, about me</h2>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="smiling face with glasses">🤓</span> I'm curiosity-driven.</h3>
      <p>Design isn't just my job, my role, or something that I'm good at. Being a designer is something that I just am, it's about the way I see the world. I'm curious by nature and I often find myself thinking about how everything around me works, and how can I make it better.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="glowing star"> 🌟</span> I'm always learning</h3>
      <p>Curiosity leads to discoveries. And discoveries lead to learning. Well, hopefully. =P Learning opens your mind, and retrofeeds curiosity. And then, as time goes by, you end up with this breadth of skills and abilities and interests and there's only so much time to do everything. But that's ok, you're a <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20191130035305/airbnb.design/defining-design-generalists/" target="_blank">Generalist</a> now; welcome to the big picture. ;)</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="orange heart">🧡</span> I'm Head of Design at JustRelate</h3>
      <p>At JustRelate, we build software that helps companies create meaningful, long-lasting customer relationships. As Head of Design, I get to combine everything I love: shaping product experiences, building and growing a design team, and having a real strategic impact on the company. It's the role I've been working towards, and I'm loving every bit of it.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="party popper">🎉</span> I celebrate Mondays</h3>
      <p>I get the people looking forward to the weekend because they can't wait to get away from their jobs. Now, don't get me wrong: I enjoy the weekends as much as the next person, but I love what I do. I look forward to Mondays to come back to work, team up with talented people, and do great stuff even greater.</p>
    </article>

  </section>

  <section id="how-i-work">

    <h2>How I like to work</h2>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="house with garden">🏡 </span>I do my best work in-house</h3>
      <p>Having worked in startups, agencies, and also with clients as a freelancer, I've found that I do my best work as an in-house designer. I like being part of a strong Design team, having ownership of the design process, and being there to see the product –and the team– grow.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="gold medal">🥇 </span>I strive for an awesome culture of work</h3>
      <p>Context shapes us, and we shape the products we build. I believe that in <span class="current-year"></span> a successful company should be like a diverse, caring, fun, playful, and hard-working community. That kind of nurturing workplace can only lead to great relationships, and great relationships lead to great products. :)</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="money bag">💰 </span>I value the work being put into products</h3>
      <p>I advocate for salary transparency; I find it ethical and practical as well. At the very least, a company shouldn't encourage salary secrecy or mind its people talking about it, because everyone should be paid fairly for their efforts. Plus, this enables people to have an overall better quality of life and they can focus on doing good work, instead of having to spend time lobbying for their compensation.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="world map">🗺️ </span>I embrace remote and hybrid working</h3>
      <p>I understand the benefits of a flexible schedule. After having experienced on-site positions, as well as hybrid and fully remote ones, I've found that while I can keep my productivity up while working from home, I do miss going every now and then to the office and spending quality time with my teammates. Also, for specific topics like hackathons or Design Sprints, it's very valuable to have a more personal approach.</p>
    </article>

  </section>

  <section id="why-me">

    <h2>What do I bring to the table?</h2>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="diamond">💎 </span>Resiliency</h3>
      <p>Born and raised in Argentina, where there's always a crisis at hand, we live our day-by-day dealing with uncertainty. We are forced to adapt and reinvent ourselves to find opportunities to grow; we even have a word for it: Opportuncrisis. I like to think about it as kind of a cultural trait: we develop resilience to high-uncertainty contexts.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="gear">⚙️ </span>Systems-oriented thinking</h3>
      <p>I see product design (and development, for that matter) holistically, with the whole being greater than the sum of its parts, and everything being deeply interconnected. I'm convinced that good design/development is scalable, and scalability needs systems and logic thinking.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="wave">🌊 </span>Adaptability</h3>
      <p>Being a fast learner (and, why not, unlearner =P) is one of my strengths. I welcome feedback to iterate myself and, though I prefer to work smart, I can roll up my sleeves and work hard when it's needed. I'm comfortable staying on the path as well as exploring wildly. I love bouncing ideas with other people, but I can do great work on my own as well, and I'm not afraid challenging the status quo when I feel a change is needed. ;)</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3><span class="emoji" role="img" aria-label="flexed biceps">🚀 </span>Team player mindset</h3>
      <p>We all know the go-to phrases about teamwork: "If you want to go fast, go alone. If you want to go far, go together.", "The whole is greater than the sum of its parts.", and so on. I know they might sound a bit cheesy, but I genuinely believe them to be true. No one alone can make a difference, together we divide our weaknesses and together we multiply our strengths.</p>
    </article>

  </section>
</Layout>
